# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# Version pins for the vanilla baseline images (CCPA arm-imx6ul and the C2Air riscv board).
# Sourced by baseline/build.sh (POSIX sh). Every tarball is fetched only by a real build, never by
# --dry-run, and is refused unless its sha256 matches the pin below.
#
# Where each hash came from. Pins first taken 2026-10-19 over HTTPS from upstream listings; all
# re-checked 2026-10-20 by a real fetch (every pin matched) and by gpg against upstream's signature
# (key fetched from the project's own site, kernel.org WKD or keyserver.ubuntu.com; fingerprints below):
#   linux       linux-7.2.10.tar.sign (over the uncompressed tar): Greg Kroah-Hartman
#               647F28654894E3BD457199BE38DBBDC86092693E; also sha256sums.asc, kernel.org autosigner
#               B8868C80BA62A1FFFAF5FDA9632D3A06589DA6B1. 7.2.10 = the LIVI pin that booted on the
#               CPC200-CCPA on 2026-10-19; 7.2.11 exists, not hardware-proven.
#   busybox     busybox-1.38.0.tar.bz2.sig: Denys Vlasenko C9E9416F76E610DBD09D040F47B70C55ACC9965B
#               (hash also in .tar.bz2.sha256)
#   dropbear    dropbear-2026.94.tar.bz2.asc and SHA256SUM.asc: F7347EF2EE2E07A267628CA944931494F29C6773
#               (the repo binary is 2026.91 at CPC200-CCPA_resources/ocbm/binaries)
#   openssh     openssh-10.6p1.tar.gz.asc: Damien Miller 7168B983815A5EEF59A4ADFD2A3F414E736060BA
#               (RELEASE_KEY.asc)
#   musl        musl-1.2.5.tar.gz.asc: 836489290BB6B70F99FFDA0556BCDB593020450F (musl.pub); LIVI's pin,
#               1.2.6 exists, not adopted
#   exfatprogs  exfatprogs-1.4.3.tar.gz.asc: Hyunchul Lee D58529CC5376E36D6E1E6F6234F230FAF78E48D3
#   mtd-utils   mtd-utils-2.3.1.tar.bz2.asc: David Oberhollenzer 13063F723C9E584AEACD5B9BBCE5DC3C741A02D1;
#               upstream publishes no sha256, the pin below was computed after that signature verified
#   regdb       wireless-regdb-2026.09.03.tar.sign: DA73759BF8619E484E5A3B47389A54219C0F2430
#               (Chen-Yu Tsai) and sha256sums.asc (kernel.org autosigner)
#   firmware    hash only (LIVI's pins; linux-firmware.git plain files carry no signature)
# Radio tools (revision 3, pinned 2026-10-20 = the latest stable release of each that day; keys from
# keyserver.ubuntu.com / keys.openpgp.org unless noted; gpg run in the Debian build chroot):
#   iw          iw-6.17.tar.sign (over the uncompressed tar): Johannes Berg, primary
#               C0EBC440F6DA091C884D8532E0F373F37BF9099A, signing subkey A5E03CB13B3733C48DDA1478D74AA23BCB0F6800
#               (GOODSIG after a refresh from keys.openpgp.org; keyserver.ubuntu.com's copy listed the subkey
#               expired); also sha256sums.asc (kernel.org autosigner, as above)
#   wpa_supplicant  wpa_supplicant-2.12.tar.gz.asc: Jouni Malinen EC4AA0A991A5F2464582D52D2B6EF432EFC895FA
#   bluez       bluez-5.87.tar.sign (over the uncompressed tar): Marcel Holtmann
#               E932D120BC2AEC444E558F0106CA9F5D1DCF2659; also sha256sums.asc (kernel.org autosigner)
#   libnl       libnl-3.12.0.tar.gz.sig: Thomas Haller 67DA3FAEBAE276BA58FC6CE314F18A98993AECD5. The signature
#               (2025-12-04) is GOOD but gpg says EXPKEYSIG: the key expired 2026-06-11, after it signed; no
#               newer copy on either keyserver. Upstream's .sha256sum file matches the pin.
#   readline    readline-8.3.tar.gz.sig and readline83-001..006.sig: Chet Ramey
#               7C0135FB088AAF6C66C650B9BB5869F064EA74AB (key from ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnu-keyring.gpg)
#   ncurses     ncurses-6.6.tar.gz.sig: Thomas E. Dickey 19882D92DDA4C400C22C0D56CC2AF4472167BE03 (GOODSIG with
#               the key from invisible-island.net, expires 2029-04-02; the copy in gnu-keyring.gpg is expired)
#   readline + ncurses exist only for BlueZ's btmgmt (its shell links readline); nothing else uses them.
# "Verified" means the signature matches a key fetched over HTTPS today; no key was checked against a
# web of trust or an out-of-band fingerprint.

